    "paragraph": "Four of today's papers carry the tag \"Urban Green Space and Health,\" focusing on indigenous knowledge and therapeutic environments, urban greening strategies for liveable cities, green infrastructure for urban wellbeing, and leveraging health and horticulture through sensory gardens. Outside this group, another paper introduced NWPU-Traffic, a large-scale remote sensing dataset with instance-level annotations for four vehicle categories across 49 cities in 7 countries. Additionally, a study of 95 cities in Japan analyzed the relationship between a postcode-level walkability index and adults' walking habits. Finally, a study of university students in Ghana examined how childhood and adolescent travel socialization influences sustainable travel preferences across different generations.",
